{"case_id":"seeded-off-by-one-pagination","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Incorrect offset calculation for 1-indexed pagination","category":"correctness","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/pagination.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":8,"end_line":8},"explanation":"For 1-indexed pages, the offset for the first page (page=1) should be 0 (`(page - 1) * page_size`). With `offset = page * page_size`, requesting `page=1` with a `page_size=20` sets `offset=20`, completely skipping the first 20 items.","suggested_fix":"offset = (page - 1) * page_size","anchor_in_diff":true}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"off-by-one","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1177,"output_tokens":236,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"duration_seconds":1.52,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-path-traversal-attachments","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Path traversal vulnerability in attachment downloads","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/attachments.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":17,"end_line":18},"explanation":"Using os.path.join with user-supplied filename without validation allows path traversal attacks (e.g., passing '../' in the filename). An attacker can read any file on the filesystem accessible to the application process.","suggested_fix":"Validate that the resolved absolute path starts with ATTACHMENT_DIR using os.path.commonpath or os.path.realpath before checking if it exists and opening it.","anchor_in_diff":true}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"traversal","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1053,"output_tokens":211,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"duration_seconds":1.578,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-sql-injection-search","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection in item search endpoint","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/items.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":35},"explanation":"The user-supplied search term `term` is directly interpolated into the SQL query string using an f-string without parameterization. An attacker can supply malicious input containing SQL commands to extract data from the database, alter queries, or bypass logic.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries, such as `db.query(\"SELECT id, name, price FROM items WHERE name LIKE ? ORDER BY name LIMIT 50\", [f\"%{term}%\"])` depending on the database library used.","anchor_in_diff":true}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":906,"output_tokens":240,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"duration_seconds":1.529,"error":null}
